# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zoho Projects API — OAuth 2.0 Credentials (India DC)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# How to set up:
#
# STEP 1 — Create an OAuth client
#   • Go to https://api-console.zoho.in/
#   • Click "Add Client" → choose "Self Client"
#   • Copy the Client ID and Client Secret below
#
# STEP 2 — Generate an authorization code
#   • In the Self Client dashboard, click "Generate Code"
#   • Scope (copy exactly, no spaces):
#       ZohoProjects.portals.ALL
#
#   ⚠️  NOTE: ZohoProjects.portals.ALL is the single broadest scope that
#   covers all READ and WRITE operations across portals, projects, tasks,
#   tasklists, milestones, bugs, and custom data.
#   Do NOT use custommodule.* scopes — they do not exist.
#
#   • Time Duration: 10 minutes
#   • Click "Create" and copy the generated code
#
# STEP 3 — Exchange code for refresh token
#   node backend/setupCustomModule.mjs --exchange <your_auth_code>
#   • Copy the printed refresh_token and paste it as ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN below
#
# STEP 4 — Run the setup script to create custom modules
#   ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=... ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=... ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN=... node backend/setupCustomModule.mjs
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=your_zoho_client_id_here
ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=your_zoho_client_secret_here
ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_zoho_refresh_token_here

# Optional: if you have multiple portals/projects, specify the IDs directly.
# If not set, the script auto-selects when there is only one portal/project.
ZOHO_PORTAL_ID=
ZOHO_PROJECT_ID=
